    "created_at": "2022-10-23T22:15:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-23T23:49:33Z",
    "body": "I simply wasn't aware it was possible at first - I've since adapted my own config with this workaround. A preset and/or documentation would certainly help other users in the future though.\r\n\r\nThat being said, I personally believe the UX would be better if you had to _opt in_ to the current behavior, for two reasons:\r\n1. I don't think this behavior is intuitive. Why would a user care about something they don't have installed? If they really do care about it, I think it's reasonable to then explicitly enable said module.\r\n2. It makes the user's config extremely verbose. For example, here's [my config](https://github.com/aw1cks-dotfiles/dotfiles/blob/676d4c6d1238fc88d40e462a920a871b9a251c53/dot_config/starship.toml). I have to reconfigure many modules that I don't use (sure, I could disable them instead of overriding the format string, but that still seems rather unnecessary). The user also has to update their config every time a new module gets added - not ideal.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
